# Phase 3 — SSH Service & Remote Access

## Practical Commands

The following commands were used during the practical lab.

### 1. Check OpenSSH Installation

```bash
# Check OpenSSH installation
sudo apt install openssh-server
```

### 2. Enable and Start SSH

```bash
# Enable and start SSH
sudo systemctl enable --now ssh
```

### 3. Check if SSH Is Active

```bash
# Check if SSH is active
systemctl is-active ssh
```

### 4. Check SSH Service Status

```bash
# Check SSH service status
sudo systemctl status ssh
```

### 5. Test SSH Connection Locally

```bash
# Test SSH connection locally
ssh localhost
```

### 6. Check Current User

```bash
# Check current user
whoami
```

### 7. Exit SSH Session

```bash
# Exit SSH session
exit
```

### 8. Stop SSH Service

```bash
# Stop SSH service
sudo systemctl stop ssh
```

### 9. Check SSH Status

```bash
# Check SSH status
sudo systemctl status ssh
```

### 10. Start SSH Service

```bash
# Start SSH service
sudo systemctl start ssh
```

### 11. Check SSH Status Again

```bash
# Check SSH status again
sudo systemctl status ssh
```

### 12. Check SSH Root Login Configuration

```bash
# Check SSH root login configuration
sudo grep PermitRootLogin /etc/ssh/sshd_config
```

### 13. Check if SSH Is Enabled

```bash
# Check if SSH is enabled
sudo systemctl is-enabled ssh
```

### 14. Check if SSH Is Active

```bash
# Check if SSH is active
sudo systemctl is-active ssh
```

### 15. List Running Services

```bash
# List running services
sudo systemctl list-units --type=service --state=running
```
